WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.100
I'm a firefighter slash EMT I recently
and recently I went on a call where a

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.940
patient didn't live not unusual by any
means

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.040
unfortunately I deal with loss of life
on almost a daily basis I detach and do

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.910
my job always working to get better this
call I failed to detach it hit me hard

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:25.619
when the patient's husband let out a
chilling let out chilling screams as his

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:30.750
thirty year old wife went from alert in
talking to dead within minutes

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.550
I let myself enter into his shoes at
that moment I got over it quick during

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.390
my days off and moved on it's part of
the job and I accept that but my

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:45.120
question is when does it become inhumane
to detach do we sometimes need to let

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.980
some weakness through to remain grounded
when dealing with such major incidents

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:58.430
as loss of life okay first of all
sympathy and empathy are not weaknesses

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:03.769
they're not weaknesses in fact it
actually takes strength to be able to

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:09.479
deal with these types of the situations
and these types of emotions the weak

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:18.630
move would actually be to cut those
emotions off completely so that being

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:27.450
said as you know obviously there is a
dichotomy because you cannot let the

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:33.270
emotions overwhelm you as a matter of
fact if you get overwhelmed by your

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:38.159
feelings then you can't do your job
properly which in its own right is

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:40.950
inhumane because now you're not able to
treat the patients that you're trying to

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.350
save because you're getting too
emotional about it

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.100
so what do you have to do the answer for
the for the millionth time of a

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.729
different subject but comes up all times
you've got to find balance you have to

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:55.590
find balance between being emotional
enough about not being too emotional you

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.540
have to learn to recognize if you're
going too far in one direction or the

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.399
other you have to do a self-assessment
you have to look and see and make sure

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:11.240
that the that you see the people you're
treating as people

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.480
you have to look at them and make sure
that you're seeing them as people that

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.220
you're not seeing them as a hunk of meat
right you have to do that you have to

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.350
make sure that you're doing that at the
same time you cannot afford emotionally

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:30.980
to go through the pain of loss every
time you see someone die cuz that's also

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.430
gonna be a problem you can't afford
emotionally to do that you can't go

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:45.290
through that pain over and over and over
again so you have to like you said you

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:50.300
have to detach normally do a good job
with that um I've seen guys get wounded

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.070
I've seen guys get killed I've been
around a lot of death and when when it

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.540
was around me I didn't have time to stop
and think about it I had to work to do

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:06.200
I had to detach myself and do my job at
the same time when it's over and that of

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.470
time was appropriate it's like you got
to connect with what happened and make

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:17.060
sure that you are dealing with it
appropriately and you know I always

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:22.340
thank firefighters and paramedics and
EMTs and and police and military but you

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.290
know paramedics and EMTs you're only
showing up if someone is in a bad way

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:32.930
and I know that's hard physically and
it's hard mentally and it's hard

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:39.200
emotionally so find a balance keep
yourself balanced make sure you're not

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:47.120
going to form one direction or the other
and thanks for doing your job man that's

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.540
like easy but sometimes you forget that
about EMTs yeah fire friendly that's the

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:59.180
only time you know where they spray I
mean pretty much yeah no getting called

